{"id":"mahabharata-12-254","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":254,"title":"चतुःपञ्चाशदधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 254 · Tuladhara's dharma of harmlessness","summary":{"en":"Tuladhara tells Jajali that there is no dharma without a cause, and that the one who gives fearlessness to all beings reaches the fearless state. He teaches that true dharma, resting on harmlessness, is hard to see but is practised by the good and the wise.","kn":"ಕಾರಣವಿಲ್ಲದ ಧರ್ಮವಿಲ್ಲ, ಎಲ್ಲ ಜೀವಿಗಳಿಗೆ ಅಭಯ ನೀಡುವವನು ಅಭಯ ಸ್ಥಾನ ತಲುಪುತ್ತಾನೆಂದು ತುಲಾಧಾರ ಜಾಜಲಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅಹಿಂಸೆಯ ಮೇಲೆ ನೆಲೆಸಿದ ನಿಜ ಧರ್ಮ ಕಾಣಲು ಕಷ್ಟ ಆದರೆ ಸಜ್ಜನರು, ಜ್ಞಾನಿಗಳು ಅದನ್ನು ಆಚರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"तुलाधार जाजलि से कहता है कि कारण के बिना कोई धर्म नहीं है और जो सब प्राणियों को अभय देता है वह अभय पद पाता है। वह सिखाता है कि अहिंसा पर टिका सच्चा धर्म देखने में कठिन है पर सज्जन और विद्वान उसका पालन करते हैं।","te":"కారణం లేని ధర్మం లేదని, అన్ని జీవులకు అభయం ఇచ్చేవాడు అభయ స్థానం పొందుతాడని తులాధారుడు జాజలితో చెబుతాడు. అహింసపై నిలిచిన నిజ ధర్మం చూడటం కష్టమైనా సజ్జనులు, జ్ఞానులు దాన్ని ఆచరిస్తారని బోధిస్తాడు.","ta":"காரணமின்றி எந்த தர்மமும் இல்லை, எல்லா உயிர்களுக்கும் அச்சமின்மை அளிப்பவன் அச்சமற்ற நிலையை அடைகிறான் என்று துலாதாரன் ஜாஜலியிடம் கூறுகிறான். அகிம்சையில் நிலைத்த உண்மையான தர்மம் காண்பது கடினம், ஆனால் நல்லோரும் அறிஞரும் அதைக் கடைப்பிடிக்கின்றனர் என்று போதிக்கிறான்.","ml":"കാരണമില്ലാതെ ധർമ്മമില്ലെന്ന് തുലാധരൻ ജാജലിയോട് പറയുന്നു; സർവ്വജീവികൾക്കും ഭയമില്ലായ്മ നൽകുന്നവൻ നിർഭയ അവസ്ഥയിലെത്തുന്നുവെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. അഹിംസയിൽ ഉറച്ച യഥാർത്ഥ ധർമ്മം കാണാൻ പ്രയാസമാണെങ്കിലും നല്ലവരും ജ്ഞാനികളും പാലിക്കുന്നതാണെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പഠിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.254; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"इत्युक्तः स तदा तेन तुलाधारेण धीमता ।\nप्रोवाच वचनं धीमाञ्जाजलिर्जपतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Addressed in this way by the wise Tuladhara, Jajali, best of those who mutter prayers, spoke to him."}},{"n":2,"text":"विक्रीणानः सर्वरसान्सर्वगन्धांश्च वाणिज ।\nवनस्पतीनोषधीश्च तेषां मूलफलानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are a merchant selling every kind of juice and perfume, plants and herbs, with their roots and fruits."}},{"n":3,"text":"अध्यगा नैष्ठिकीं बुद्धिं कुतस्त्वामिदमागतम् ।\nएतदाचक्ष्व मे सर्वं निखिलेन महामते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whence did you come by this settled, final wisdom? Tell me all of it fully, O man of great mind."}},{"n":4,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तुलाधारो ब्राह्मणेन यशस्विना ।\nउवाच धर्मसूक्ष्माणि वैश्यो धर्मार्थतत्त्ववित् ।\nजाजलिं कष्टतपसं ज्ञानतृप्तस्तदा नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus questioned by the renowned brahmin, the vaishya Tuladhara, who knew the truth of dharma and profit, spoke on the subtleties of dharma to Jajali, hard in austerity, O king, he being content with knowledge."}},{"n":5,"text":"वेदाहं जाजले धर्मं सरहस्यं सनातनम् ।\nसर्वभूतहितं मैत्रं पुराणं यं जना विदुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jajali, I know the eternal dharma with its secrets, kind to all beings, the ancient dharma that people know."}},{"n":6,"text":"अद्रोहेणैव भूतानामल्पद्रोहेण वा पुनः ।\nया वृत्तिः स परो धर्मस्तेन जीवामि जाजले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Living by a way that harms no creature, or harms only slightly, is the highest dharma; by that I live, Jajali."}},{"n":7,"text":"परिच्छिन्नैः काष्ठतृणैर्मयेदं शरणं कृतम् ।\nअलक्तं पद्मकं तुङ्गं गन्धांश्चोच्चावचांस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"With cut wood and grass I have made this shop, and I deal in lac, padmaka, tall aromatics and perfumes of all grades."}},{"n":8,"text":"रसांश्च तांस्तान्विप्रर्षे मद्यवर्जानहं बहून् ।\nक्रीत्वा वै प्रतिविक्रीणे परहस्तादमायया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahmin sage, I buy many kinds of juices, except liquor, and sell them again, taking from others' hands without deceit."}},{"n":9,"text":"सर्वेषां यः सुहृन्नित्यं सर्वेषां च हिते रतः ।\nकर्मणा मनसा वाचा स धर्मं वेद जाजले ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who is always a friend to all and devoted to the good of all, in act, thought and word, knows dharma, Jajali."}},{"n":10,"text":"नाहं परेषां कर्माणि प्रशंसामि शपामि वा ।\nआकाशस्येव विप्रर्षे पश्यँल्लोकस्य चित्रताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I neither praise nor curse others' deeds, but watch the world's variety as if from the sky, O sage."}},{"n":11,"text":"नानुरुध्ये विरुध्ये वा न द्वेष्मि न च कामये ।\nसमोऽस्मि सर्वभूतेषु पश्य मे जाजले व्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not favor or oppose, hate or desire; I am even toward all beings. See my vow, Jajali."}},{"n":12,"text":"इष्टानिष्टविमुक्तस्य प्रीतिरागबहिष्कृतः ।\nतुला मे सर्वभूतेषु समा तिष्ठति जाजले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Freed from liking and disliking, and without attachment or affection, my scale stands level toward all beings, Jajali."}},{"n":13,"text":"इति मां त्वं विजानीहि सर्वलोकस्य जाजले ।\nसमं मतिमतां श्रेष्ठ समलोष्टाश्मकाञ्चनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Know me thus, Jajali, best of the wise: the same to the whole world, seeing clod, stone and gold alike."}},{"n":14,"text":"यथान्धबधिरोन्मत्ता उच्छ्वासपरमाः सदा ।\nदेवैरपिहितद्वाराः सोपमा पश्यतो मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Just as the blind, deaf and mad live ever bound to their breath alone, their doors shut by the gods, so is the comparison with me as I look on."}},{"n":15,"text":"यथा वृद्धातुरकृशा निःस्पृहा विषयान्प्रति ।\nतथार्थकामभोगेषु ममापि विगता स्पृहा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the old, sick and wasted lose longing for sense objects, so my longing for wealth, desire and enjoyment too has gone."}},{"n":16,"text":"यदा चायं न बिभेति यदा चास्मान्न बिभ्यति ।\nयदा नेच्छति न द्वेष्टि तदा सिध्यति वै द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a person fears nothing and nothing fears him, when he neither wishes nor hates, then the twice-born attains perfection."}},{"n":17,"text":"यदा न कुरुते भावं सर्वभूतेषु पापकम् ।\nकर्मणा मनसा वाचा ब्रह्म संपद्यते तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"When one bears no evil intent toward any being in deed, thought or word, then he becomes fit for Brahman."}},{"n":18,"text":"न भूतो न भविष्यश्च न च धर्मोऽस्ति कश्चन ।\nयोऽभयः सर्वभूतानां स प्राप्नोत्यभयं पदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is no dharma, past or future, like this: one who is fearless toward all beings reaches the state of fearlessness."}},{"n":19,"text":"यस्मादुद्विजते लोकः सर्वो मृत्युमुखादिव ।\nवाक्क्रूराद्दण्डपारुष्यात्स प्राप्नोति महद्भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One from whom the whole world shrinks as from the jaws of death, through cruel speech and harsh punishment, meets great fear."}},{"n":20,"text":"यथावद्वर्तमानानां वृद्धानां पुत्रपौत्रिणाम् ।\nअनुवर्तामहे वृत्तमहिंस्राणां महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We follow the conduct of the elders, with sons and grandsons, who live rightly, the great-souled who do no harm."}},{"n":21,"text":"प्रनष्टः शाश्वतो धर्मः सदाचारेण मोहितः ।\nतेन वैद्यस्तपस्वी वा बलवान्वा विमोह्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The eternal dharma has been lost, confused by mere customary practice; by that even a physician, ascetic or strong man is deluded."}},{"n":22,"text":"आचाराज्जाजले प्राज्ञः क्षिप्रं धर्ममवाप्नुयात् ।\nएवं यः साधुभिर्दान्तश्चरेदद्रोहचेतसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"By right conduct, Jajali, a wise man quickly attains dharma, if he lives self-controlled among the good with a heart free of malice."}},{"n":23,"text":"नद्यां यथा चेह काष्ठमुह्यमानं यदृच्छया ।\nयदृच्छयैव काष्ठेन संधिं गच्छेत केनचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As a log carried along in a river by chance may by chance meet another log,"}},{"n":24,"text":"तत्रापराणि दारूणि संसृज्यन्ते ततस्ततः ।\nतृणकाष्ठकरीषाणि कदा चिन्नसमीक्षया ।\nएवमेवायमाचारः प्रादुर्भूतो यतस्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and other pieces, straw, wood and dung join it from here and there, unplanned, so did this conduct arise from here and there."}},{"n":25,"text":"यस्मान्नोद्विजते भूतं जातु किंचित्कथंचन ।\nअभयं सर्वभूतेभ्यः स प्राप्नोति सदा मुने ॥","meaning":{"en":"He from whom no creature is ever in any way alarmed always gains fearlessness from all creatures, sage."}},{"n":26,"text":"यस्मादुद्विजते विद्वन्सर्वलोको वृकादिव ।\nक्रोशतस्तीरमासाद्य यथा सर्वे जलेचराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"From whom the whole world shrinks, learned one, as from a wolf, as water creatures all flee when someone stands on the bank shouting,"}},{"n":27,"text":"सहायवान्द्रव्यवान्यः सुभगोऽन्योऽपरस्तथा ।\nततस्तानेव कवयः शास्त्रेषु प्रवदन्त्युत ।\nकीर्त्यर्थमल्पहृल्लेखाः पटवः कृत्स्ननिर्णयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"those with helpers, with wealth, the fortunate and others: the poets in the scriptures speak of these, and the clever, who write on a few words for fame, claim complete decision."}},{"n":28,"text":"तपोभिर्यज्ञदानैश्च वाक्यैः प्रज्ञाश्रितैस्तथा ।\nप्राप्नोत्यभयदानस्य यद्यत्फलमिहाश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever fruit one here enjoys through austerities, sacrifices, gifts and wise words, the same is the fruit of the gift of fearlessness."}},{"n":29,"text":"लोके यः सर्वभूतेभ्यो ददात्यभयदक्षिणाम् ।\nस सर्वयज्ञैरीजानः प्राप्नोत्यभयदक्षिणाम् ।\nन भूतानामहिंसाया ज्यायान्धर्मोऽस्ति कश्चन ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who gives all beings the gift of fearlessness in the world gains that gift of fearlessness as though he had sacrificed with every rite; no dharma is greater than non-harming of beings."}},{"n":30,"text":"यस्मान्नोद्विजते भूतं जातु किंचित्कथंचन ।\nसोऽभयं सर्वभूतेभ्यः संप्राप्नोति महामुने ॥","meaning":{"en":"He from whom no creature is ever alarmed in any way gains fearlessness from all creatures, great sage."}},{"n":31,"text":"यस्मादुद्विजते लोकः सर्पाद्वेश्मगतादिव ।\nन स धर्ममवाप्नोति इह लोके परत्र च ॥","meaning":{"en":"He from whom the world shrinks as from a snake in the house gains no dharma, in this world or the next."}},{"n":32,"text":"सर्वभूतात्मभूतस्य सम्यग्भूतानि पश्यतः ।\nदेवापि मार्गे मुह्यन्ति अपदस्य पदैषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For one who sees all beings as his own self and views creatures rightly, even the gods are confused on the path, seeking the footprint of the footless."}},{"n":33,"text":"दानं भूताभयस्याहुः सर्वदानेभ्य उत्तमम् ।\nब्रवीमि ते सत्यमिदं श्रद्दधस्व च जाजले ॥","meaning":{"en":"They say the gift of safety to creatures is the best of all gifts. I tell you this truth; believe it, Jajali."}},{"n":34,"text":"स एव सुभगो भूत्वा पुनर्भवति दुर्भगः ।\nव्यापत्तिं कर्मणां दृष्ट्वा जुगुप्सन्ति जनाः सदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"The same man who was fortunate becomes unfortunate again; seeing the misfortune that follows deeds, people always feel disgust."}},{"n":35,"text":"अकारणो हि नेहास्ति धर्मः सूक्ष्मोऽपि जाजले ।\nभूतभव्यार्थमेवेह धर्मप्रवचनं कृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even the subtlest dharma here, Jajali, is not without cause; the teaching of dharma was made for the welfare of beings, present and future."}},{"n":36,"text":"सूक्ष्मत्वान्न स विज्ञातुं शक्यते बहुनिह्नवः ।\nउपलभ्यान्तरा चान्यानाचारानवबुध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Being subtle, it cannot easily be known, and it has many concealments; one grasps other practices only after finding something in between."}},{"n":37,"text":"ये च छिन्दन्ति वृषणान्ये च भिन्दन्ति नस्तकान् ।\nवहन्ति महतो भारान्बध्नन्ति दमयन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some castrate bulls and some pierce their noses, they load them with heavy burdens, tie and tame them."}},{"n":38,"text":"हत्वा सत्त्वानि खादन्ति तान्कथं न विगर्हसे ।\nमानुषा मानुषानेव दासभोगेन भुञ्जते ॥","meaning":{"en":"They kill creatures and eat them; why do you not condemn them? Men even enjoy other men as slaves."}},{"n":39,"text":"वधबन्धविरोधेन कारयन्ति दिवानिशम् ।\nआत्मना चापि जानासि यद्दुःखं वधताडने ॥","meaning":{"en":"By killing, binding and opposing they make them work day and night; you yourself know the pain of killing and beating."}},{"n":40,"text":"पञ्चेन्द्रियेषु भूतेषु सर्वं वसति दैवतम् ।\nआदित्यश्चन्द्रमा वायुर्ब्रह्मा प्राणः क्रतुर्यमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All divinity dwells in beings with five senses: the sun, moon, wind, Brahma, life-breath, sacrifice and Yama."}},{"n":41,"text":"तानि जीवानि विक्रीय का मृतेषु विचारणा ।\nका तैले का घृते ब्रह्मन्मधुन्यप्स्वौषधेषु वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having sold those living beings, what is the care for dead ones? What does it matter about oil, ghee, honey, water or herbs, brahmin?"}},{"n":42,"text":"अदंशमशके देशे सुखं संवर्धितान्पशून् ।\nतांश्च मातुः प्रियाञ्जानन्नाक्रम्य बहुधा नराः ।\nबहुदंशकुशान्देशान्नयन्ति बहुकर्दमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cattle raised happily in a place without gadflies and mosquitoes, dear to their mothers, men drive by force to places full of gadflies, thin grass and mud."}},{"n":43,"text":"वाहसंपीडिता धुर्याः सीदन्त्यविधिनापरे ।\nन मन्ये भ्रूणहत्यापि विशिष्टा तेन कर्मणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Draft animals tormented by loads sink down unlawfully; I think even killing an embryo is not worse than that deed."}},{"n":44,"text":"कृषिं साध्विति मन्यन्ते सा च वृत्तिः सुदारुणा ।\nभूमिं भूमिशयांश्चैव हन्ति काष्ठमयोमुखम् ।\nतथैवानडुहो युक्तान्समवेक्षस्व जाजले ॥","meaning":{"en":"They think farming good, yet that livelihood is very cruel: the iron-tipped wooden plough kills the earth and the creatures lying in it. Look likewise at the yoked oxen, Jajali."}},{"n":45,"text":"अघ्न्या इति गवां नाम क एनान्हन्तुमर्हति ।\nमहच्चकाराकुशलं पृषध्रो गालभन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cows are called \"not to be killed\"; who may kill them? Nahusha did a great wrong, like a locust attacking a flame."}},{"n":46,"text":"ऋषयो यतयो ह्येतन्नहुषे प्रत्यवेदयन् ।\nगां मातरं चाप्यवधीर्वृषभं च प्रजापतिम् ।\nअकार्यं नहुषाकार्षीर्लप्स्यामस्त्वत्कृते भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sages and ascetics told Nahusha this: \"You killed the cow, mother, and the bull, the lord of creatures. Nahusha, you did a forbidden thing; through you we shall have fear.\""}},{"n":47,"text":"शतं चैकं च रोगाणां सर्वभूतेष्वपातयन् ।\nऋषयस्ते महाभागाः प्रजास्वेव हि जाजले ।\nभ्रूणहं नहुषं त्वाहुर्न ते होष्यामहे हविः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They brought down a hundred and one diseases on all beings, those glorious sages, on the creatures, Jajali. They called Nahusha an embryo-killer: \"We will not offer oblations to you.\""}},{"n":48,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा ते महात्मानः सर्वे तत्त्वार्थदर्शिनः ।\nऋषयो यतयः शान्तास्तरसा प्रत्यवेदयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said so, those great-souled seers of the truth of things, the calm ascetics, swiftly made this declaration."}},{"n":49,"text":"ईदृशानशिवान्घोरानाचारानिह जाजले ।\nकेवलाचरितत्वात्तु निपुणान्नावबुध्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Such inauspicious, terrible practices exist here, Jajali, but because you only follow custom you do not discern them skillfully."}},{"n":50,"text":"कारणाद्धर्ममन्विच्छेन्न लोकचरितं चरेत् ।\nयो हन्याद्यश्च मां स्तौति तत्रापि शृणु जाजले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seek dharma by reason; do not simply follow the world's custom. Hear this too, Jajali: whether one kills me or praises me,"}},{"n":51,"text":"समौ तावपि मे स्यातां न हि मे स्तः प्रियाप्रिये ।\nएतदीदृशकं धर्मं प्रशंसन्ति मनीषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"both would be the same to me, for I have neither liking nor disliking. Such a dharma the wise praise."}},{"n":52,"text":"उपपत्त्या हि संपन्नो यतिभिश्चैव सेव्यते ।\nसततं धर्मशीलैश्च नैपुण्येनोपलक्षितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is complete with reasoning, followed by ascetics, always practiced by those devoted to dharma, and recognized through skill."}}]}]}